Question 3 — Mixed Concepts

Using the employees and departments tables:

Find the highest-paid employee in each department. 
If multiple employees have the same highest salary, return all of them.


WITH RankedEmployees AS (
    SELECT
        CONCAT(e.FirstName, ' ', COALESCE(e.LastName, '')) AS EmployeeName,
        d.DepartmentName,
        e.Salary,
        DENSE_RANK() OVER (
            PARTITION BY e.DepartmentID
            ORDER BY e.Salary DESC
        ) AS SalaryRank
    FROM employees e
    JOIN departments d
        ON e.DepartmentID = d.DepartmentID
)
SELECT
    EmployeeName,
    DepartmentName,
    Salary
FROM RankedEmployees
WHERE SalaryRank = 1;
